    <briefdescription>
<para>The name of a test case, with the location of its definition. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The first parameter of <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1suite_1a402696dc4d4978ff3c050427890cfe01" kindref="member">suite::test()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case_1aac23ee148d8e5946cd87e0de036e9fb8" kindref="member">test_case::test()</ref></computeroutput>. The constructors are not explicit, so a string literal, a <computeroutput>const char*</computeroutput>, or a <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput> passed as the test case name converts implicitly; the default argument of the constructors is evaluated at the place of the conversion, which is the call to <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput> in the user code, so the location of the test case is captured without an additional argument (which could not follow the variadic arguments of <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput>).</para>
<para>The location is used to report a failure that is not associated with a check, such as an exception escaping the test case body.</para>
<para>The name is not copied. Since the test cases run immediately, within the call to <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput>, a temporary string passed as the argument, which lives until the end of the full expression, remains valid while the test case runs; a named <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case__name" kindref="compound">test_case_name</ref></computeroutput> object must not outlive the string it was constructed from.</para>
<para>A <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput> is not accepted, since it is not guaranteed to be null-terminated; pass <computeroutput>std::string (sv)</computeroutput> instead.</para>
<para>Since a conversion sequence may include only one user-defined conversion, an argument that converts to <computeroutput>const char*</computeroutput> or to <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput> via a user-defined conversion operator must be converted explicitly.</para>
<para>A helper function that adds test cases on behalf of its caller can take a <computeroutput>const <ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case__name" kindref="compound">test_case_name</ref>&amp;</computeroutput> parameter and pass it to <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput>, so that the reported location is that of the call to the helper, not that of the call to <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput> inside the helper.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">check_answer<sp/>(mt::suite&amp;<sp/>ts,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>mt::test_case_name&amp;<sp/><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case__name_1a624bdd72fd18db434a64993818bb5466" kindref="member">name</ref>,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>v)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>ts.test<sp/>(<ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case__name_1a624bdd72fd18db434a64993818bb5466" kindref="member">name</ref>,<sp/>[v]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{<sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(v,<sp/>42));<sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
